			<div class="content" id="post-content-3921886">
									

<p>This sentence from the containment procedures:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Civilians entering these programs are to have their backgrounds checked for previous forklift certification that was previously revoked.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Seems to be in conflict with this one from the description:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In addition, all evidence that the target was ever forklift certified will be voided in some way during this event.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Surely the background check won't find anything if all the evidence is gone? Unless I'm misunderstanding what's meant by &quot;voided&quot; here.</p>
<p>Also, I don't get the flawed teaching. If people fail their test then their certification is revoked, they have good reason to believe it actually happened, and soon enough you've got headlines like &quot;Aliens Revoked My Forklift Certification!!&quot;. If people pass then they can easily shrug the whole thing off as a dream.</p>
<p>That stuff aside, I really love the concept of the Health and Safety Aliens taking over through Improved Forklift Operation.</p>

